 ``run()`` is context-sensitive. For example, commands placed before ``.python_packages()`` are executed before installing Python dependencies, while those placed after are executed after installation. This allows you to perform certain tasks in the correct order.
 
+``build_include()``
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Include additional files from your build context in the image. The paths you pass are relative to the Bento context root (typically the directory where your ``service.py`` resides). Each included file is copied into the image under ``./src/<name>``. It supports chaining with other methods.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    import bentoml
+
+    image = bentoml.images.Image(python_version='3.11') \
+        .build_include("data/", "config.yaml")
+
+This is useful when your Service needs files at runtime that are not Python packages, such as model artifacts, configuration files, or data directories.
+
 ``run_script()``
